name: design-taste-frontend
description: Anti-slop frontend skill for landing pages, portfolios, and redesigns. The agent reads the brief, infers the right design direction, and ships interfaces that do not look templated.

# Design Taste Frontend Skill

## Overview
A specialized frontend design skill that prevents generic AI-looking interfaces by enforcing design principles, typography discipline, color calibration, and layout diversification. Works for landing pages, portfolios, and redesigns.

## Key Features
- **Brief Inference Engine**: Automatically reads design brief signals (page kind, vibe words, audience, brand assets)
- **Three Design Dials**: DESIGN_VARIANCE (1-10), MOTION_INTENSITY (1-10), VISUAL_DENSITY (1-10)
- **Design System Mapping**: Maps briefs to real design systems (Fluent, Carbon, Material, shadcn/ui, etc.)
- **Anti-Pattern Enforcement**: Blocks common AI tells (purple gradients, glassmorphism spam, centered hero defaults)
- **Pre-Flight Check**: 50+ point checklist before shipping any design

## Configuration
The skill uses three dials that can be overridden conversationally:
- `DESIGN_VARIANCE: 8` (1=Perfect Symmetry, 10=Artsy Chaos)
- `MOTION_INTENSITY: 6` (1=Static, 10=Cinematic)
- `VISUAL_DENSITY: 4` (1=Airy, 10=Packed)

## When to Use
- Building new landing pages, portfolios, marketing sites
- Redesigning existing websites (preserve or overhaul modes)
- Creating premium SaaS, agency, or editorial interfaces
- Any frontend work where visual quality matters

